What is Personalized mRNA Cancer Vaccine Therapy?
Personalized mRNA Cancer Vaccine Therapy represents a breakthrough in oncology treatment by leveraging each patient's unique tumor profile. These vaccines analyze tumor tissue samples to identify specific mutations and protein expressions, then use mRNA technology to instruct immune cells to target these cancer-specific antigens. The highly tailored approach has shown promise in clinical trials for both solid tumors (like melanoma and lung cancer) and non-solid tumors (including certain leukemias).
Unlike traditional cancer treatments, these vaccines stimulate the body's immune system to recognize and attack cancer cells while minimizing damage to healthy tissue. Leading pharmaceutical companies including Moderna and BioNTech are advancing this technology, building on their mRNA platform expertise from COVID-19 vaccine development.
